## Armbands

| Prop models | What it is |
|---|---|
| `p_poggy_armband_medic_s1` … `_s9` | White cloth with a sewn-on red cross |
| `p_poggy_armband_mourning_s1` … `_s9` | Plain black cloth |
| `p_poggy_armband_posse_s1` … `_s9` | White cloth printed "Posse" between two stars |
| `p_poggy_armband_quarantine_s1` … `_s9` | Yellow cloth printed "Quarantine" |
| `p_poggy_armband_press_s1` … `_s9` | White cloth printed "Press" |

An armband goes on an arm bone, and the game cannot scale a prop, so each armband comes in
nine sizes (`_s1` smallest, `_s9` largest; the elbow end is a little narrower than the
shoulder end). In Poggy Badge 1.4.0 or newer, give its grade:

```lua
prop  = "p_poggy_armband_medic_s3",
bone  = "SKEL_L_UpperArm",   -- or SKEL_R_UpperArm
sizes = { "p_poggy_armband_medic_s1", "p_poggy_armband_medic_s2", "p_poggy_armband_medic_s3",
          "p_poggy_armband_medic_s4", "p_poggy_armband_medic_s5", "p_poggy_armband_medic_s6",
          "p_poggy_armband_medic_s7", "p_poggy_armband_medic_s8", "p_poggy_armband_medic_s9" },
```

Players then pick the size that fits their outfit with the editor's Size slider.

The models are made by `toolsadge-props` (Blender, then Sollumz_RDR and CodeX).
